<p data-end=\"9576\" data-start=\"9552\"><strong>4-FSPASSENGERS &amp; ACARS</strong></p>

<p data-end=\"9876\" data-start=\"9578\"><strong>a) FsPassengers:</strong><br data-end=\"9597\" data-start=\"9594\" />
For FsPassengers users (FS2004/FSX), after multiple attempts, we could not resolve some communication bugs between Prométhée and FsPassengers. For now, FsPassengers will not be used with the management system. Note: this does not replace submitting flight reports on Prométhée.</p>

<p data-end=\"10096\" data-start=\"9878\"><strong>b) ACARS</strong>:<br data-end=\"9890\" data-start=\"9887\" />
With the latest Prométhée version, the vmsACARS module will be available for live flight tracking and automated flight report management.<br data-end=\"10030\" data-start=\"10027\" />
More information will be provided once Prométhée is operational.</p>

<p data-end=\"10116\" data-start=\"10099\"><strong>5-WHY PROMETHEUS</strong></p>

<p data-end=\"10146\" data-start=\"10118\"><strong>a) The \"Prometheus\" system:</strong></p>

<p data-end=\"10246\" data-start=\"10148\">Prometheus&nbsp;is the company’s economic and flight management system. It allows, among other things:</p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<ul>
	<li data-end=\"10306\" data-start=\"10250\">Member management: registration, removal, status, etc.</li>
	<li data-end=\"10455\" data-start=\"10309\">Fleet management: Full fleet management including each individual registration and status (availability, maintenance, failures, location, etc.).</li>
	<li data-end=\"10587\" data-start=\"10458\">Economic management: fuel prices, salaries, loans, maintenance, miscellaneous costs, company economic reports, statistics, etc.</li>
	<li data-end=\"10681\" data-start=\"10590\">Flight management: based on available aircraft, destinations, flight offers/demands, etc.</li>
	<li data-end=\"10725\" data-start=\"10684\">Flight tracking, performance, and more.</li>
</ul>

<p></p>

<p data-end=\"10751\" data-start=\"10727\"><strong>b) A bit of \"history\":</strong></p>

<p data-end=\"11108\" data-start=\"10753\">In Greek mythology, Prometheus is a Titan, son of Iapetus and Themis, brother to Atlas, Menoetius, and Epimetheus. Father of Deucalion with Pronoia. He is called \"Titan Prometheus\" as the son of a Titan and a Titaness.<br data-end=\"10974\" data-start=\"10971\" />
Being immortal by birth, he holds the rank of a primordial deity (Titans were giant primordial deities preceding the Olympian gods).</p>

<p data-end=\"11312\" data-start=\"11110\">Prometheus created man from a lump of clay, with Athena breathing life into it. She taught him astronomy, navigation, mathematics, and other arts, which he shared with humans despite Zeus’ opposition.</p>

<p data-end=\"11618\" data-start=\"11314\">When Zeus took fire from mankind, Prometheus, aided by Athena, stole it back from Olympus and gave it to humans. To punish him, Zeus sent Pandora to Epimetheus, Prometheus’ brother. Pandora was created by Hephaestus at Zeus’ request, beautiful but foolish, cruel, and lazy. Epimetheus politely refused.</p>

<p data-end=\"11992\" data-start=\"11620\">Angered, Zeus chained Prometheus to Mount Caucasus, where a Griffin-vulture devoured his liver daily. His suffering was endless as his liver regenerated each night.<br data-end=\"11787\" data-start=\"11784\" />
Moved by his brother’s fate, Epimetheus married Pandora, who soon opened the jar Prometheus had struggled to contain, releasing evils afflicting mankind: aging, work, disease, madness, vice, and passion.</p>

<p data-end=\"12232\" data-start=\"11994\">Heracles freed Prometheus during his twelve labors, but to honor Zeus’ vow that the Titan remain chained, Prometheus had to wear an iron ring from his chains attached to a piece of Caucasus rock—this was the first ring set with a stone.</p>

<p data-end=\"12520\" data-start=\"12234\">Gaston Bachelard, under the name \"Prometheus Complex,\" defined it as \"All tendencies that push us to know as much as our fathers, more than our fathers, as much as our masters, more than our masters.\" He also said, \"The Prometheus complex is the Oedipus complex of intellectual life.\"</p>

<p data-end=\"12556\" data-start=\"12523\">c) So why the name \"Prométhée\"?</p>

<p data-end=\"12578\" data-start=\"12558\">For these reasons:</p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<p></p>

<ul>
	<li data-end=\"12683\" data-start=\"12582\">Just as Prometheus the Titan is immortal, Air Inter is immortal in our hearts, a Titaness of sorts…</li>
	<li data-end=\"12791\" data-start=\"12686\">Just as Prometheus created man, Air Inter gave birth to our \"life\" as children: the passion for flying…</li>
	<li data-end=\"12870\" data-start=\"12794\">Just as Prometheus taught humans, Air Inter trained generations of pilots…</li>
	<li data-end=\"12974\" data-start=\"12873\">Just as Prometheus stole fire from Zeus, Air Inter never feared fighting giants for what was right…</li>
	<li data-end=\"13069\" data-start=\"12977\">Just as Prometheus had his liver devoured daily, Air Inter continues despite life’s blows…</li>
	<li data-end=\"13168\" data-start=\"13072\">Just as Prometheus and Pandora’s jar, Air Inter preserved French aviation as much as possible…</li>
	<li data-end=\"13260\" data-start=\"13171\">Just as Prometheus kept his ring, Air Inter bore the colors of injustice until its end…</li>
	<li data-end=\"13377\" data-start=\"13263\">Finally, like the \"Prometheus Complex,\" aviation-wise, we always seek to go further in the pursuit of knowledge…</li>
</ul>

<p></p>

<p data-end=\"13474\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\" data-start=\"13379\">Thus, \"Prometheus\" is the perfect name for a system that helps preserve the memory of Air Inter!</p>

